From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: retry accesses behind duplicate heap faults

A second fault on a heap region that an earlier fault already mapped
returns without an MMU command, so the access stays stalled until the
job times out. Flush the region as the mapping did so the access
retries, as kbase does with an UNLOCK.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -649,7 +649,8 @@ static int panfrost_mmu_map_fault_addr(struct panfrost
 
 	sgt = &bo->sgts[page_offset / (SZ_2M / PAGE_SIZE)];
 	if (sgt->sgl) {
-		/* Pages are already mapped, bail out. */
+		/* Mapped by an earlier fault, flush so the stalled access retries */
+		panfrost_mmu_flush_range(pfdev, bomapping->mmu, addr, SZ_2M);
 		goto out;
 	}
 
